            "lens": "review-reliability",
            "findings": [],
            "evidence": [
              "Reviewed all four changed paths in full. In gitexec.go, Standing handles a detached HEAD, a missing default branch, and malformed git output through explicit paths: it returns a partial result for the first two and an error for malformed output.",
              "defaultBranch rejects origin/HEAD names containing glob characters. Tips are sorted and deduplicated, so the ^tip exclusions are deterministic.",
              "standing_test.go covers the main shapes of history: own commits, the default branch itself, merges in both directions, detached HEAD, a master default, no default branch, origin/HEAD naming, and remote-ahead and local-ahead defaults. It also covers malformed git output through a fake runner, and the error text it expects matches the message commitNames produces.",
              "fakes_test.go adds a Standing fake that honors its failure injection, and the app.go interface addition is consistent with the adapter's signature.",
              "The only gaps are minor: no test for an unborn HEAD, and none for a shallow clone. Neither leaves the introduced behavior unproved."
            ]
          }
        }
      }
